  "about": "Judged queries for TestRetrievalQuality. key = the best sources for the question (the API doc, the reference tutorial, the thread that has the fix); relevant = useful but secondary. Judged by reading each candidate from three independent paths, then pooled — the top 10 of each ranking variant tried was judged too, so a variant that surfaces relevant documents the baseline missed isn't scored as if it surfaced noise: the hybrid top 30, the BM25 top 15, and a title search over the non-Discord sources. Built against the v2.2 corpus (66,023 docs); a doc_id missing from the db fails the test, so a rebuilt corpus that renames documents shows up instead of silently scoring zero.",
